A||||17||jg88gt||Installing 3800 SC in one of my 88 GT's||||7||
Z||000000||jg88gt||10-31-2001||11:46 PM||||Started installing a 3800 SC in my car, the motor is out of a GTP with 1900 miles on it. We are using a Haltech computer to run this set-up with a 5 speed. Here's some pictures.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/101-0164a_IMG.jpg"> <BR>   Motor coming out<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/101-0171a_IMG.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/101-0172a_IMG.jpg"> <BR>3800 SC almost ready to go in.<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/101-0197a_IMG.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/101-0172a_IMG_1.jpg"> <BR>Almost done, post more as we go along.<P><BR>[This message has been edited by jg88gt (edited 11-01-2001).]<P>[This message has been edited by jg88gt (edited 11-01-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by jg88gt (edited 11-01-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000001||fieroX||11-01-2001||02:17 AM||||first off, welcome to the forum.  <BR>Looks like your project is coming right along.  I have a few questions for you from things I see in your pictures.  I notice in the second pic down the aluminum torque strut mount has been moved to the other side of the engine, did you have to fab anything up for this to go on the other side?  Do you plan to attach another mount to the trunk side firewall for the dogbone mount?  why I ask is because I am currently undertaking the same engine swap, but my engine is torn apart at the moment, and I was wondering since the engine is going to torque to the back of the car, it will push on the mount instead of pulling.  Are you going to put some kind of mount on the frontside of the engine?  and in the same pic I notice a black mount that comes off the side of the supercharger and to the alternator, what is this?  is it stock? My engine doesnt have this.  <BR>I like how you did the paintjob making it look like a 2.8, thats cool.<BR>Also which haltech are you using the 6gm?  I was wondering about that but on haltechs website It said up to 1992 gm v6 cars.  <BR>You might want to keep an eye out for <A HREF="http://www.animuLPerformance.com" TARGET=_blank>www.animuLPerformance.com</A>  they are starting to make some pretty unique aftermarket high performance parts for these engines.  Nothing is available yet, but when the stuff is its going to be awesome!<P>thanks for any additional info you can provide, and good luck!  see ya around the forum, this place is great.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fierox.com/logo2small.gif"> ||||reg||1
