Z||000006||MinnGreenGT||11-01-2001||05:15 PM||||Nice... but <B>PLEASE</B> replace your pics with the ones I just uploaded (don't worry, all I did was resize them...)<P>Just edit your post and change your codeline to have a "sm" at the end of each title (right before the ".jpg")<P>Example: "101-0164_IMG_5sm.jpg"<P>This will make it [b]much[b] easier for others to view this post.  Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000007||jg88gt||11-01-2001||08:30 PM||||The pictures you uploaded didn't seem to work when I changed the titles. I'll go ahead and resize them when I get a chance. <BR>The answers to everyone else's questions are coming when I get a chance.||||reg||1
Z||000008||jg88gt||11-01-2001||11:04 PM||||To answer a few of the question that were asked above.<P>1) The oil filter adapter is GM#24501300 there is an adapter that hooks to it if you want to add a remote oil cooler. I'll get the part number and post it.<P>2) I am using a RAM clutch and pressure plate, I'll see how it will holdup. RAM is manufactured here in Columbia, SC a few miles from where we live. Went over and talked to their tech folks a few times and was told it would work with the HP.<P>3)On the aluminum torque strut mount in the second picture, I was just playing with different locations to mount the strut. The 3800 motor rotates the same as the 2.8 and it's mounted on that side. Since mounting the motor I have made my own torque strut mount and will post pictures once finished.<P>4)The black mount that comes off the side of the supercharger to the alternator is stock .<P>5) The Haltech computer is a E6GM, I've talk to the folks at Haltech and this was what they recommended. I had to make my own wiring harness... just used the ends from the stock 88 GT and the 3800 SC wiring harness.<P>6) The headers are from CWest||||reg||6
